cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ElectroSim-LSV-RRDE-Analyzer"
abstract: >-
  A Streamlit application for electrochemical polarization data: automated
  ohmic-drop (iR) compensation of linear-sweep voltammetry (LSV) data using
  the uncompensated resistance (Ru) estimated from an EIS Nyquist-arc circle
  fit; LSV analysis (onset potential, benchmark overpotentials, Tafel slope,
  with RHE reference-electrode conversion and mechanistic interpretation);
  Koutecký–Levich analysis of multi-rotation-rate RDE data; and ORR/RRDE
  analysis (onset/half-wave potential, electron-transfer number, and
  peroxide yield from ring-disk data).
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
